# =============================================================================
# SwasthyaSetu AI — environment variables (EXAMPLE ONLY — no real values)
#
# Copy this file to .env.local for local development:
#     cp .env.example .env.local
# Then replace every "replace-with-..." placeholder with your own value.
#
# NEVER commit .env.local or any file containing a real key/password.
# In production these same names are set in the Vercel project settings
# (see README.md → "USER LIVE STEPS"). Server-only variables must NEVER use
# the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix — anything prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ is sent to the
# browser.
#
# "Used by current code" = the name is read by the code in this repo today.
# "Production target"    = the name is reserved for the production build
#                          described in docs/STACK_DECISIONS.md; production
#                          code must read exactly this name. Do not invent a
#                          differently-spelled alias.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NODE_ENV is normally set by Next.js / Vercel automatically
# (development locally, production on Vercel). You usually do NOT set it by
# hand. It is listed here only so nobody invents a custom mode flag.
# NODE_ENV=development

# Optional display/debug version string for this deployment. Not read by
# current code.
APP_VERSION=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Postgres (Supabase) — Drizzle / `pg` — server only
#
# Current-code names, keep them EXACT:
#   src/db/index.ts        reads SQL_HOST, SQL_DB_NAME, SQL_USER, SQL_PASSWORD
#                          (isSqlConfigured = SQL_HOST && SQL_DB_NAME are set;
#                           if either is missing the app falls back to the
#                           dev-only in-memory store)
#   src/db/drizzle.config.ts reads SQL_HOST, SQL_DB_NAME,
#                          SQL_ADMIN_USER, SQL_ADMIN_PASSWORD
# For Supabase, SQL_HOST / SQL_USER / SQL_PASSWORD come from the Supabase
# dashboard → Project Settings → Database (use the connection-pooler host
# your project offers). Ask your database provider which host/user to use —
# do not guess a hostname.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SQL_HOST=replace-with-database-host
# Optional. Current code does not pass a port to `pg`, so the `pg` default
# (5432) applies. Reserved so production code can set the pooler port
# explicitly; if production code reads a port it must use this name.
SQL_PORT=5432
SQL_USER=replace-with-database-user
SQL_PASSWORD=replace-with-database-password
SQL_DB_NAME=replace-with-database-name

# Drizzle Kit / migration tooling only (src/db/drizzle.config.ts).
# Use a privileged database user here — never reuse it as SQL_USER for the
# running app if the provider lets you separate them.
SQL_ADMIN_USER=replace-with-database-admin-user
SQL_ADMIN_PASSWORD=replace-with-database-admin-password

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase — server only
# Production target (Supabase Auth + Postgres). Current prototype code does
# not read these yet: auth today is demo tokens / Firebase — see
# docs/STACK_DECISIONS.md.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_URL=replace-with-supabase-project-url
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=replace-with-supabase-anon-key
# SECRET. Server only. Bypasses Row-Level Security — never expose it to the
# browser, never prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_, rotate it if it ever leaks
# (see docs/DATA_PROTECTION.md → key-rotation checklist).
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=replace-with-supabase-service-role-key
# Alternative / complement to the service-role key for verifying Supabase
# Auth access tokens on the server (JWKS endpoint of your Supabase project).
# Only needed if the production auth code verifies JWTs via JWKS instead of
# calling Supabase. Leave blank if not used.
SUPABASE_JWKS_URL=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase — browser-safe copies (public by design)
# These two ARE sent to the browser. The anon key is only safe because
# Row-Level Security is enabled on every table. Never put the service-role
# key, SQL_PASSWORD, GEMINI_API_KEY or any SMS key in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=replace-with-supabase-project-url
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=replace-with-supabase-anon-key

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gemini — supplemental explanation text ONLY — server only
# Current code: app/api/ai-explain/route.ts reads GEMINI_API_KEY.
# Gemini never decides the triage category — the deterministic screening
# engine does (see docs/STACK_DECISIONS.md). If the key is missing/blank the
# route returns a deterministic fallback note and screening still works.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
GEMINI_API_KEY=replace-with-gemini-api-key
# app/api/ai-explain/route.ts reads this name; when unset it defaults to
# gemini-2.5-flash in code.
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notifications (referral / follow-up alerts) — production target, server only
# Current code sends NO real notifications. Production code must read
# NOTIFICATIONS_MODE and use exactly these names.
#   log     = write the notification to the server log only (default, safest)
#   webhook = POST the notification to NOTIFICATION_WEBHOOK_URL
#   sms     = send an SMS via the SMS_* settings below
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTIFICATIONS_MODE=log
NOTIFICATION_WEBHOOK_URL=
# Optional bearer token sent with the webhook POST. Server only.
NOTIFICATION_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=

# SMS provider (Twilio-compatible shape). Only used when
# NOTIFICATIONS_MODE=sms. Server only — never expose these to the browser.
# Remember: patient records store a phone's last 4 digits ONLY, so an SMS to
# a patient cannot be addressed from a patient record alone — see
# docs/DATA_PROTECTION.md.
SMS_API_URL=
SMS_API_KEY=replace-with-sms-api-key-when-sms-is-enabled
SMS_FROM=replace-with-sender-id-or-number
